# Only CMakeLists.txt, src/, and test/ are actually needed to build the image (Dockerfile's
# COPY . . + cmake/make -j2, which builds the xv6_tests target from test/*.cpp too). Everything
# else here is host-side tooling/docs/config that has zero effect on the compiled binaries but,
# without this file, still busts COPY's cache layer on every edit and forces a full ~4-5min
# rebuild - see performance.md's router_cpp Docker build-cache trap note.
build_router.md
stress_run.sh
run_test.sh
monitor.sh
monitor/
start.sh
stop.sh
test_csv_files/
create_cpp_router_from_java
config/
build_local/
